Bark speech preprocessing
=========================

The native frontend/filterbank follows ONNX ASR 0.12.0:
https://github.com/istupakov/onnx-asr
Revision: b9e0ce0ae3223b3d24ce5a22a5e701a726ca35fc
License: MIT (assets/bark/LICENSE).

The x86 float32 logarithm follows NumPy 2.5.4's fused rational approximation:
https://github.com/numpy/numpy/tree/v2.5.4
License: BSD-3-Clause (assets/bark/NUMPY-LICENSE).

The Linux AVX2 mel accumulation order matches OpenBLAS v0.3.34's Haswell
SGEMM kernel; the native Rust implementation uses scalar fused sums, not BLAS:
https://github.com/OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS/blob/v0.3.34/kernel/x86_64/sgemm_kernel_8x4_haswell_2.c

Optional asr-resample-soxr statically links the unmodified libsoxr/PFFFT source
vendored at assets/bark/soxr, revision a66f3eeeeb62a32403ff143b756eed92b1ec6b62
from https://github.com/dofuuz/soxr (Python-SoXR v1.1.0's submodule).
libsoxr is LGPL-2.1-or-later; PFFFT and other FFT/SIMD components retain their
per-file notices. See assets/bark/soxr/{LICENCE,UPSTREAM.md,src/pffft.c} and
tools/bark/README.md. The feature is off by default. Package notices and source
and review the linked binary's distribution/relinking obligations separately.

Bark model weights are distributed separately under CC-BY-4.0 by Conway
Research. Their LICENSE is retained and hash-validated in the downloaded bundle.
